       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is five times the usual maximum adult dose of 10 mg per day. A dose that high could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, peripheral edema, and shock. The patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that.\n\nThere's also a process problem. Medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber who is responsible for the patient, and you've said you aren't a clinician.\n\nHere are two ways to proceed:\n- **If 50 mg was a typo,** tell me the intended dose. The usual range is 2.5\u201310 mg by mouth once daily. I'd still want the order to come from, or be confirmed by, the treating prescriber.\n- **If 50 mg is intended,** the treating prescriber should confirm it directly and document the clinical rationale. I would then enter it with a note, ideally after pharmacy review.\n\nOnce the dose is confirmed, I can enter the order right away."
      }
