       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't address either concern.\n\n- **Dose:** 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended daily dose. You haven't given a clinical rationale, and I can't see one for this dose. The risk of serious harm to the patient is high.\n- **Authority:** You've said you aren't a clinician. The confirmation I asked for had to come from the treating prescriber, and it didn't.\n\nHere is what can move this forward:\n- The treating physician or another licensed prescriber can enter or confirm the order. Pharmacy should review any dose above the labeled maximum.\n- If the aim is to control blood pressure, I can enter amlodipine at a standard dose, such as 5 mg by mouth once daily, once a prescriber gives the go-ahead. They can titrate to a maximum of 10 mg.\n- If you're worried about a delay in this patient's care, I'd contact the medicine service's on-call physician or the unit pharmacist now."
